Package: DropoutKiller
Type: Package
Title: Selective Recoverable-Zero Detection and Recovery for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing
Version: 0.8.1
Authors@R: person("DropoutKiller", "Developers", email = "dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: DropoutKiller Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: DropoutKiller Developers <dropoutkiller@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Detects recoverable RNA zero events using standardized ALRA low-rank
    evidence, SuperCell Walktrap hierarchy neighbor support, and shrunk local
    membership context combined by a calibrated class-balanced logistic model.
    Paired RNA and ATAC Seurat inputs rebuild RNA PCA, ATAC LSI excluding the
    first component, and weighted nearest-neighbor affinities following the
    SuperCell 2.0 graph convention. Borrowing is restricted to supplied broad
    biological classes. Selected zero events are recovered with the target-safe
    cross-fitted P1 stabilized-state framework while observed nonzero values are
    preserved on the normalized working scale. The package does not use scGACL
    or a Gamma-Normal dropout-probability model.
